() Tj T*
(1. PROJECT SUMMARY) Tj T*
(HyeScriptures is a scripture reading and study application built as a TypeScript/React web app,) Tj T*
(with a Capacitor Android wrapper. Its product surface combines Bible reading, study utilities,) Tj T*
(personal spiritual journals, audio and speech tools, community features, learning games, AI-backed) Tj T*
(assistance, user progress, and tier-gated features. Supabase provides authentication and cloud) Tj T*
(functionality; local browser storage and bundled data support important client-side experiences.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Repository facts) Tj T*
(- Public repository; default branch main; description: Bible; no declared license or topics.) Tj T*
(- Configured web homepage: https://hye-scriptures.vercel.app) Tj T*
(- Capacitor app ID: com.hyescriptures.app; app name: Hyescriptures; web output: dist.) Tj T*
(- Root includes React/Vite/TypeScript source, Android native project, Supabase functions/migration,) Tj T*
(  static PWA/offline assets, and an Android GitHub Actions workflow.) Tj T*
(- GitHub language byte counts: TypeScript 2,030,788; CSS 518,603; JavaScript 12,443;) Tj T*
(  Java 5,291; HTML 2,833. These are GitHub byte-based estimates, not line counts.) Tj T*
(- Approximate share: TypeScript 79.0%, CSS 20.2%, JavaScript 0.5%, Java 0.2%, HTML 0.1%.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Interpretation: this is a substantial, feature-rich application rather than a standalone Bible text) Tj T*
(viewer. The source tree includes dedicated product modules and data for reading, study, social,) Tj T*
(personal organization, gamification, mobile support, and server-side AI/payment handling.) Tj T*
