(3. PLATFORM, DATA AND SERVICE DESIGN) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Client and mobile) Tj T*
(- React 19, TypeScript, Vite 8, and ES modules are declared in package.json.) Tj T*
(- Capacitor 8 dependencies include Android, Filesystem, and Share. Android native source and) Tj T*
(  Gradle wrapper are checked into android/; a custom AppIcon Java plugin is present.) Tj T*
(- public/ contains a web manifest, service worker, offline fallback, favicon, app icons, and) Tj T*
(  theme-specific icon assets. useOffline and cache utilities indicate offline support.) Tj T*
(- Native file/share integration supports exporting content or assets from mobile.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Backend and persistence) Tj T*
(- Supabase JS client reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. Auth and application) Tj T*
(  services use this client; server-side logic lives in Supabase Edge Functions.) Tj T*
(- Edge Functions in-tree: ai, daily_devotional, paystack-webhook, scripture, and sermon.) Tj T*
(- The AI and sermon functions provide server-side generation endpoints; daily_devotional provides) Tj T*
(  devotional content generation; paystack-webhook handles payment-provider callbacks.) Tj T*
(- A SQL migration defines user_stats, ai_usage_logs, reading_progress, and sermon_generations,) Tj T*
(  with RLS policies and indexes. Policies generally scope reads/writes to auth.uid(); AI usage) Tj T*
(  mutation is intended for service-side handling.) Tj T*
(- SyncContext triggers an initial sync and recurring sync for signed-in users, stops syncing on) Tj T*
(  sign-out, and attempts a sync when the app returns online. Failures are intentionally silent.) Tj T*
(- Some app content/preferences are stored in localStorage. cache.ts and SyncContext implement cloud) Tj T*
(  synchronization; storage.ts includes bookmark, highlight, and history helpers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Commercial/access model) Tj T*
(- TierGate, UpgradePage, useSubscription, and useAILimits implement feature access and upgrade UX.) Tj T*
(- Types include free/pro/elder plan values; the app shell prominently labels the elder tier.) Tj T*
(- Payment integration is indicated by the Paystack webhook function. This report does not infer a) Tj T*
(  complete payment flow or deployment configuration from the presence of that handler alone.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Important scope note: features listed here are confirmed by named code modules and configuration.) Tj T*
(The presence of a component does not guarantee every external service is configured, deployed, or) Tj T*
(available in production. No live production verification was performed for this report.) Tj T*
